course: dictionary
lesson: 13667
title: Informed: knowing the facts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Informed comes from the verb inform, which means to tell someone facts or news. When you are informed, someone has told you something important. «The school informed the parents about the trip.» The parents now know the facts about the trip.
explain: As an adjective, informed means knowing a lot about a subject. «Mia is well-informed about dinosaurs; she has read every book in the library.» The clue is well-informed: Mia has good facts in her head about dinosaurs.
explain: An informed choice is one made using facts. «After reading both reports, the class made an informed decision about the new park.» The choice was not a lucky guess. Ask yourself: did they use facts to decide?
explain: Be careful: inform on means something different. It means secretly telling the police or someone in charge about another person's wrongdoing. «The thief was caught after a friend informed on him.» The words caught and thief are the clues that this is about wrongdoing.
fact: Informed means told facts or news, or knowing a lot about a subject.
fact: «Keep someone informed» means keep telling them the news as it happens.
fact: «Well-informed» means having good information about a subject.
fact: «An informed choice» is a choice made using facts.
fact: «Inform on» means secretly telling the police or someone in charge about another person's wrongdoing.
exercise: «The school informed the parents about the trip.» What does informed mean here? | Forgot about the parents | Wrote a poem for the parents | *Told the parents the facts | Gave the parents a present
exercise: «Mia is well-informed about dinosaurs.» What does well-informed mean? | Is afraid of dinosaurs | Can run very fast | *Knows a lot about dinosaurs | Has never seen a dinosaur
exercise: «The class made an informed decision after reading both reports.» Why was the decision informed? | *It was made using facts from the reports | It was made without reading anything | It was made quickly for fun | It was made by flipping a coin
test: «Please keep me informed about the bus times.» What does keep me informed mean? | Keep my bus ticket safe | *Keep telling me the news about the bus times | Keep me in the dark about the bus times | Keep the bus times a secret
test: «The thief was caught after a friend informed on him.» What does informed on mean here? | Gave him a present | Asked him about the weather | Helped him escape | *Secretly told the police about his wrongdoing
exam: «Ben made an informed choice about his pet by reading three books first.» What makes his choice informed? | He flipped a coin to decide | He asked his friend to choose | *He read books to get facts before choosing | He chose the cheapest pet in the shop
